CORE thorough-paths no-new-smt broken-smt-backend wide-pointer-encoding
test.c
--wide-pointer-encoding --no-simplify --unwind 301 --object-bits 8 --no-malloc-may-fail
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^too many addressed objects
--
Issue #881: with the wide pointer encoding a pointer carries a full flat
address rather than a packed object identifier, so the --object-bits
limit no longer bounds the number of addressable objects. This program
allocates 300 distinct objects under --object-bits 8; the standard
encoding rejects it with "too many addressed objects" (EXIT=6, see
test.desc), whereas the wide encoding verifies it successfully.
